Description: Tracks played for 30 s are greyed out until their stick is ejected
 Like the played history on a Pioneer player: once a track has played on a
 deck for 30 s (counted while the deck is playing, reset when the deck loads
 a different track), every track list draws it in the played-track colour
 (WTrackTableView's trackPlayedColor, #555555 by default). It stays grey
 until the USB stick it is on is ejected or pulled, or Mixxx restarts.
 .
 New XdjPlayedTracks singleton (src/library/xdjplayedtracks.{h,cpp}) keeps
 the set of played file locations in memory, measured on a 1 s timer from
 [ChannelN],play and PlayerInfo's loaded track. BaseTrackTableModel checks a
 row's location in its ForegroundRole, after the missing-file colour, and
 repaints when the set changes. LibraryControl drops a stick's entries when
 its umount succeeds and when the mount poll sees the slot go away. Nothing
 is written to the library: Mixxx's own "played" flag (which rekordbox
 lists do not have, and which would outlive the stick) is untouched.
